  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-crypto-portfolio",
      "text": "English | [中文](README.zh.md)\n\nA free, 100% self-hosted [DeepSeek Harness](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness) (DSH) plugin that unifies your **on-chain and CEX assets** into one self-contained web dashboard.\n\n**Requires** `dsh` `0.1.1-rc.2` (Node `^22.19 || >=24`) · Python 3.9+ · `pip3 install requests pynacl`\n\n```sh\ndsh plugin --profile demo add dsh-crypto-portfolio   # npm\ndsh --profile demo                                    # dashboard at http://127.0.0.1:8080\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh-crypto-portfolio",
      "text": "> **Twin project.** This dashboard is the twin of the [SmartFolio Chrome extension](https://chromewebstore.google.com/detail/smartfolio/ogiijkjoahbekjnjhnchjefllioelcin): the extension puts the same wallets in your toolbar, this one is the self-hosted, all-chains view that runs on your own machine. Same idea, two shells — the dashboard is a DSH plugin and follows the DSH plugin conventions, so it keeps its own name."
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh-crypto-portfolio",
      "text": "> Unofficial project, independently developed and maintained by community members.\n\n---"
    },
    {
      "section": "Why it exists / The pain points",
      "text": "I built it because the pain points are real."
    },
    {
      "section": "1 · My money lives in seven places, and checking the total means opening six pages",
      "text": "EVM assets in DeBank, SOL and staking on-chain, BTC in a block explorer, plus Binance / Bybit / Backpack / OKX / Bitget — each with its own app. Checking \"how much do I actually have\" meant hopping between six pages, and it was easy to miss a wallet along the way.\n\n**This plugin puts all of it on a single screen.**"
    },
    {
      "section": "2 · Assets that block explorers can't see",
      "text": "Some money is genuinely invisible: native Solana stake accounts (`getParsedStakeAccounts` misses them), Hyperliquid L1 staked HYPE and spot balances, exchange earn/funding accounts. None of these are plain SPL/ERC-20 tokens, so ordinary tools never read them.\n\n**This plugin digs them out and prices them into your total** — including the 12.1 SOL staked in the account above and the ~318 HYPE staked on Hyperliquid."
    },
    {
      "section": "3 · Dust coins and phishing tokens inflate the numbers",
      "text": "DeBank lists plenty of fake tokens — ETHG, for example, is a **phishing token with a manipulated price** that once inflated one account by $570K.\n\n**One-click blacklisting**: every token you blacklist is removed from totals, trends and historical snapshots instantly."
    },
    {
      "section": "4 · \"How much did I have last week?\"",
      "text": "Without history there's no peace of mind.\n\n**Every refresh saves the last snapshot of the day** (SQLite, deduplicated by day); over time it draws a trend line that is uniquely yours:\n\n---"
    },
    {
      "section": "What it does",
      "text": "- **A zero-dependency web dashboard, launched from a real DSH plugin.** No framework, no CDN — Python stdlib + vanilla JS.\n- **Covers BTC / EVM / Solana / Dogecoin / Cardano / Hyperliquid L1 / CEX.** DeBank's 73 chains, BTC P2SH+P2TR, native Solana staking, Dogecoin (BlockCypher), Cardano (Koios, incl. stake addresses), Hyperliquid's official API (staked HYPE + spot + perp equity + vault equity), and read-only CEX keys (named `<exchange>_read`). Five exchanges are supported (Binance, Bybit, Backpack, OKX, Bitget). Read-only CEX keys cover spot, OKX's funding sub-account and Backpack's futures collateral account, including tokenised equities; on Bitget the spot account is summed with the real futures accounts and the `S*` demo products are skipped, so play money never enters the total.\n- **Global filters.** Category (BTC / EVM / Solana / Dogecoin / Cardano / CEX), wallet and chain dropdowns drive every panel — total, wallet-share pie, trend, chain distribution, token table.\n- **Up to five block explorers per wallet.** Each wallet card ends in a row of explorer icons — the provider this app actually reads from comes first (DeBank · bitaps · Jupiter · Dogechain · Cardanoscan), then th"
    },
    {
      "section": "What it does",
      "text": "Every box in the diagram is a real data pipeline:"
    },
    {
      "section": "How it integrates with DSH",
      "text": "Not a wrapper — a real plugin:\n\nThe dashboard also watches its own Python sources: editing `tracker/*.py` restarts\nit within a couple of seconds (same process, no DSH restart), and static files are\nread from disk on every request, so a UI change is a page reload. Settings → Service\nhas a *Restart the service* button for the cases where you want to force it."
    },
    {
      "section": "How it integrates with DSH",
      "text": "- Declares a `dsh.bundle` manifest (`cordis.patch.yml`), so it installs with `dsh plugin add`.\n- `apply(ctx)` hooks into the Cordis lifecycle: seeds user-local `profiles/default` from public templates on first run, spawns the dashboard as a child process, and stops it cleanly on `ctx.on('dispose')`.\n- Exposes JSON APIs (`GET /api/refresh`, `/api/history`, `/api/tokens`, ...) that an agent can call directly, in addition to the web UI."
    },
    {
      "section": "Privacy (important)",
      "text": "This repository contains **no private keys, no private wallets, no balances** — `tracker/config.py` ships with `WALLETS = []` and empty keys. All private configs live in git-ignored local `profiles/`. Clone it, review it, run it with confidence."
    },
    {
      "section": "Requirements",
      "text": "- **`dsh` `0.1.1-rc.2`** (or a compatible release within the same pre-release line)\n  and **Node `^22.19.0 || >=24.0.0`** — the range DSH itself declares.\n- **Python 3.9+** with two pip packages:\n\n```sh\n  pip3 install requests pynacl\n  ```\n\nThese are ordinary runtime dependencies, not vendored, so `pip` can pick the\n  build that matches your platform."
    },
    {
      "section": "From npm (recommended)",
      "text": "Installs prebuilt code and needs **no build permission**:\n\n```sh\ndsh plugin --profile demo add dsh-crypto-portfolio\ndsh --profile demo\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "From a tarball (offline / air-gapped)",
      "text": "```sh\npnpm pack                                    # produces dsh-crypto-portfolio-0.1.0.tgz\ndsh plugin --profile demo add ./dsh-crypto-portfolio-0.1.0.tgz\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "From GitHub",
      "text": "```sh\ndsh plugin --profile demo add github:0xRabit/dsh-crypto-portfolio#<commit-sha>\n```\n\nThis package is plain JavaScript + Python with **no build step**, so its\n`prepare` is a no-op and pnpm does not need you to allowlist a build script —\nunlike plugins that ship TypeScript sources. Pin a commit SHA anyway, so a\nlater push cannot change what runs on your machine."
    },
    {
      "section": "Verify the layer before booting",
      "text": "```sh\ndsh --profile demo --dump-config      # look for: # == dsh-crypto-portfolio\n```\n\nIf that line is missing, the bundle did not activate — the package installed as a\nplain dependency instead. Re-run the `add` and check the warning it printed."
    },
    {
      "section": "Override the port",
      "text": "A patch replaces the whole `config` of a row, so restate every key you need.\nPut this in `$DSH_HOME/profiles/demo/cordis.patch.yml`:\n\n```yaml\n- id: portfolio-tracker\n  name: dsh-crypto-portfolio\n  config:\n    port: 8199\n\nOr set `PORTFOLIO_PORT` in the environment."
    },
    {
      "section": "Standalone (no DSH)",
      "text": "```sh\npython3 run.py --init-template --port 8080   # seeds profiles/default from public templates\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Layout",
      "text": "```\nprofiles/default/   sources.json + wallets.json (public template, auto-seeded)\ntemplates/          public example configs (no secrets)\ntracker/            backend fetchers (debank/btc/solana/hyperliquid/cex/prices)\nstatic/             web dashboard (vanilla JS, no external deps)"
    },
    {
      "section": "Releasing",
      "text": "One command from the maintainer's working tree (the release scripts live there, not in\nthis published bundle), and the flow is deliberately split in two:\n\n```sh\nscripts/sync_public.sh --push                 # publish code — the version does NOT move\nscripts/sync_public.sh --push --release       # bump + tag + refresh every market listing\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Releasing",
      "text": "| Action | Version | Changelog | Tag | Market listings |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `--push` | unchanged | unchanged | — | untouched |\n| `--push --release` | bumped | `[Unreleased]` stamped | `vX.Y.Z` | branch pushed, PR prepared per market |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Releasing",
      "text": "- **A push is not a release.** Publishing code leaves `package.json` exactly as it is, so\n  installed users see no update until a version is cut on purpose.\n- **A release refreshes every listing.** The wording for each market lives here, under\n  [`market/`](market/), so it is versioned with the code it describes and always matches\n  the version being shipped. A market whose text did not change is skipped instead of\n  getting an empty pull request."
    },
    {
      "section": "Releasing",
      "text": "| Market | How it is fed | What the release does |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| [awesome-dsh-plugin](https://github.com/awesome-dsh-plugin/awesome-dsh-plugin) | one YAML file per plugin | [`market/awesome-dsh-plugin.yml`](market/awesome-dsh-plugin.yml) → `data/plugins/0xRabit__dsh-crypto-portfolio.yml` |\n| [awesome-deepseek-harness](https://github.com/awesome-deepseekharness/awesome-deepseek-harness) | curated bilingual tables | [`market/awesome-deepseek-harness.json`](market/awesome-deepseek-harness.json) → the row in each language's `🧩 Tools, Workflows & Presets` table |\n| [awesome-dsh-hub](https://github.com/ukinch605/awesome-dsh-hub) | hourly scrape of the `dsh-plugin` topic | nothing to submit — the release only verifies the entry is present and current |"
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "MIT — see [LICENSE](LICENSE)."
    }
